From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] config_base/config_3/config_4: ChromeOS/WhaleOS LXC config fixes

1. Remove lxc.hook.post-stop = /dev/null: ChromeOS has noexec semantics
   on /dev/null, causing "Permission denied" when LXC tries to execute it
   as a post-stop hook script.

2. Move proc/sys mounts from lxc.mount.auto to explicit mount entries.
   Makes the mount configuration explicit and predictable on ChromeOS.

3. Remove lxc.apparmor.profile and lxc.seccomp.profile from config_3:
   ChromeOS LXC is built without AppArmor and seccomp support; these
   options cause a fatal parse error ("Built without AppArmor support").

4. Remove lxc.seccomp.allow_nesting = 1 from config_4: same reason.

--- a/data/configs/config_base
+++ b/data/configs/config_base
@@ -7,12 +7,14 @@

 lxc.cap.keep = audit_control sys_nice wake_alarm setpcap setgid setuid sys_ptrace sys_admin wake_alarm block_suspend sys_time net_admin net_raw net_bind_service kill dac_override dac_read_search fsetid mknod syslog chown sys_resource fowner ipc_lock sys_chroot

-lxc.mount.auto = cgroup:ro sys:ro proc
+lxc.mount.auto = cgroup:ro

 lxc.console.path = none

 lxc.include = /var/lib/waydroid/lxc/waydroid/config_nodes
 lxc.include = /var/lib/waydroid/lxc/waydroid/config_session

-lxc.hook.post-stop = /dev/null

+
+lxc.mount.entry = proc proc proc nosuid,nodev,noexec,create=dir 0 0
+lxc.mount.entry = sysfs sys sysfs nosuid,nodev,noexec,ro,create=dir 0 0
--- a/data/configs/config_3
+++ b/data/configs/config_3
@@ -1,7 +1,5 @@
 lxc.uts.name = waydroid
 
-lxc.apparmor.profile = unconfined
-lxc.seccomp.profile = /var/lib/waydroid/lxc/waydroid/waydroid.seccomp
 
 lxc.no_new_privs = 1
 
--- a/data/configs/config_4
+++ b/data/configs/config_4
@@ -1,2 +0,0 @@
-lxc.seccomp.allow_nesting = 1
-
